---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | ClearCalc Tools"
  description="Privacy policy for ClearCalc Tools. Calculator inputs stay in the browser. Hosting logs, cookies, and Google advertising cookies are explained, with opt-out links."
>
  <section class="legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: November 10, 2026.</p>
    <p>This policy describes how ClearCalc Tools (clearcalctools.com) handles information when you use the site. The site is operated by Zayed, an individual, who can be reached at <a href="mailto:zayed70010@gmail.com">zayed70010@gmail.com</a>. ClearCalc does not require an account.</p>
    <h2>Calculator inputs</h2>
    <p>Each calculator runs in your browser. When you press Calculate, the page applies the formula on that page to the values in the form and shows the result on the same page. Those values are not sent to a ClearCalc server, stored in an account, or written into a ClearCalc database. The pages do not save calculator inputs in browser storage. You need JavaScript for a result to appear. ClearCalc does not receive a copy of the numbers you type.</p>
    <h2>What the site collects</h2>
    <p>The pages you load do not include an analytics script. There is no Google Analytics tag, no tag manager, and no other traffic-measurement script in the site. ClearCalc does not receive a report of which pages you opened.</p>
    <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like other hosts, Cloudflare can process technical connection data needed to deliver and protect the site, such as your IP address, the browser type you send, the URL you request, and the time of the request. ClearCalc's pages do not add a separate analytics feed on top of that. Cloudflare's own privacy notice is at <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a>. Those logs may be processed in the United States or in other countries where the host operates.</p>
    <p>If you email <a href="mailto:zayed70010@gmail.com">zayed70010@gmail.com</a>, the message contains your email address and whatever you chose to write, which may include calculator inputs you paste in. That message is used to reply and to look into an error, a suggestion, or a partnership note. It is not sold.</p>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>ClearCalc's own pages do not set a cookie to remember you, to measure an audience, or to store an account. The calculators do not need a cookie to run. The host may set a cookie that is strictly necessary to deliver or secure the connection. You can block or delete cookies in your browser. Blocking a strictly necessary host cookie can affect whether the site loads, and it does not change the calculator math.</p>
    <h2>Advertising cookies</h2>
    <p>ClearCalc does not currently place an advertising script on these pages, and it does not have an ads.txt file. No advertisement is served from this site's code today. The rest of this section is the rule for advertising cookies, including any Google advertising cookies this site may use.</p>
    <p>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a person's prior visits to this website and to other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users based on their visit to this site and other sites on the Internet.</p>
    <p>You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Ads Settings</a>. How Google uses advertising cookies is explained at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses advertising cookies</a>. You can opt out of some other third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.</p>
    <h2>Selling and sharing</h2>
    <p>ClearCalc does not sell personal information. It does not share personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising today, because no advertising script is installed. If advertising cookies are added later, that use can count as a "share" under California law. You can use the opt-out links above, and you can email <a href="mailto:zayed70010@gmail.com">zayed70010@gmail.com</a> with the subject "Do not sell or share my personal information". That request will be honored.</p>
    <h2>How long information is kept</h2>
    <p>Calculator inputs are not kept by ClearCalc at all. Hosting logs are kept by the host for its own security and reliability periods. Email you send is kept long enough to answer you and to fix or consider the point you raised, and then deleted when it is no longer needed for that, unless a longer period is required by law.</p>
    <h2>United Kingdom and European rights</h2>
    <p>If you are in the United Kingdom or the European Economic Area, you can ask what personal information is held about you, ask for a copy, ask for a correction, or ask for it to be deleted. You can object to processing based on legitimate interests, ask for a restriction, and, where the law gives it, ask for information you provided to be sent to you or to someone else. You can also complain to a supervisory authority. In the UK that is the Information Commissioner's Office, at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>.</p>
    <p>In plain terms, the site relies on legitimate interests to let the host keep connection logs so the pages stay available and secure, and on the message you send when you email for help. Calculator inputs are handled on your device and are not a record ClearCalc collects. To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:zayed70010@gmail.com">zayed70010@gmail.com</a>. There is no separate data-protection officer.</p>
    <h2>California rights</h2>
    <p>If you are a California resident, you can ask ClearCalc to tell you the categories and specific pieces of personal information collected about you, the sources, the purpose, and the categories of third parties it is disclosed to. You can ask for deletion. You can ask ClearCalc not to sell or share your personal information. You will not be treated differently for asking. The categories this site can hold are identifiers in an email you send (your email address and the contents of the message) and internet activity the host records in a connection log (such as IP address and the page requested). ClearCalc does not sell that information.</p>
    <p>Send a request to <a href="mailto:zayed70010@gmail.com">zayed70010@gmail.com</a>. Say that you are making a California privacy request, and say whether you want to know, delete, or opt out of sale or sharing. An authorized agent may email for you if you say so in the message and the agent provides enough for Zayed to confirm the request is yours. The same address works if you live somewhere else and want to make a similar request.</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>ClearCalc is written for adults doing everyday calculations. It is not directed at children under 13, and it does not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child has emailed personal information, write to <a href="mailto:zayed70010@gmail.com">zayed70010@gmail.com</a> and ask for it to be deleted.</p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the "Last updated" date at the top of this page will change with it. A material change to advertising or analytics will be described here before that service is turned on.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Privacy questions and requests go to <a href="mailto:zayed70010@gmail.com">zayed70010@gmail.com</a>. You can also start from the <a href={`${base}contact/`}>contact page</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
